    "created_at": "2015-09-28T15:23:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-28T15:23:30Z",
    "body": "Yeah, that would be better, I think. There's no internal concept for what `navigator.userAgent` returns, OK to just say \"If the User-Agent header contains the string 'WebKit' ...\" or similar? That would make the Gecko case look like the default although it's in the minority, but I don't think that's a big issue.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
